WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.000
Lesson 2.3 · Theory of Change
Inputs

2
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:11.800
Inputs are the resources your activities need, including your own unpaid time.

3
00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:25.541
Inputs are the resources your activities need: people and their skills, money, space, equipment, IT and technology, transport, partners, permissions and information. Unpaid time, including your own, counts too.

4
00:00:25.941 --> 00:00:26.541
Have, need and limits

5
00:00:26.541 --> 00:00:37.130
What you have: Resources already in hand, including your own and volunteers’ time. For example: Two founders’ time, ten years of baking skill and a friend’s van on Saturdays.

6
00:00:37.130 --> 00:00:46.978
What you still need: Gaps you must still secure; at the start, most inputs are gaps. For example: A shared-kitchen slot, insurance and four trainees still to recruit.

7
00:00:46.978 --> 00:01:00.989
Limits: Constraints such as time, permissions or rules on how a resource can be used. For example: The kitchen is free only in the mornings, and the youth fund cannot pay for equipment.

8
00:01:01.389 --> 00:01:01.989
Kinds of inputs to check

9
00:01:01.989 --> 00:01:08.774
People and skills: founders, trainees, mentors, volunteers, and what they know how to do.

10
00:01:08.774 --> 00:01:16.300
Space, equipment, IT and transport: a kitchen, a mixer, a card reader, a van on Saturdays.

11
00:01:16.300 --> 00:01:24.085
Money, partners and permissions: savings and a grant, the youth centre, insurance and registration.

12
00:01:24.485 --> 00:01:25.085
Why they matter

13
00:01:25.085 --> 00:01:30.389
1. Honest gaps show what you must build before you launch.

14
00:01:30.389 --> 00:01:36.063
2. Unpaid time is real; leaving it out hides the true cost.

15
00:01:36.063 --> 00:01:42.367
3. Matching resources to activities shows whether your scope is realistic.

16
00:01:42.767 --> 00:01:43.367
What they guide

17
00:01:43.367 --> 00:01:48.670
1. Your internal objectives: how you will build the missing inputs.

18
00:01:48.670 --> 00:01:54.344
2. Your budget, where you will cost them properly in Module 9.

19
00:01:54.344 --> 00:02:01.019
3. A smaller first scope if one founder holds too many roles.

20
00:02:01.419 --> 00:02:02.019
What to avoid

21
00:02:02.019 --> 00:02:06.952
Leaving out unpaid time from founders, volunteers or members.

22
00:02:06.952 --> 00:02:12.256
Mixing what you have with what you hope to get.

23
00:02:12.256 --> 00:02:18.559
Planning activities nobody has the time or skills to run.

24
00:02:19.159 --> 00:02:20.959
You list your inputs, what you already have and the gaps.

25
00:02:20.959 --> 00:02:24.959
Then save it, and download it as a PDF.

26
00:02:26.459 --> 00:02:29.559
Method into Impact
Better foundations. Stronger organisations.
